i also thought the whetstone idea (various implementations) was interesting.
having a 3rd grey stone would enrich the strategy regarding luck/loadstones.
i don't see having additional adjectives such as sharp/dull on weapons as
really beneficial. the blessed/cursed modes handle this well already.

a curious note: there is a hacker in our playground who was considered the
best rogueist around (often went to level 28 just for kicks!). when we
switched to hack he was completely mystified, complaining that the rest of
us had some inside knowledge or knew special tricks (not the case). around
about the time of nethack2.3 this hacker was ready to call it quits on hack
since he had never won another game in over 2 years! with the advent of
nethack3.0 this hacker is back!! he's finally won a game again (demi-god) and
his comments are that this new hack is the easiest game around. he
doesn't have (or want) access to source code. on the other hand there
are a couple of hackers who have had scores in the 6 and 7 Meg range
in nethack2.3 who can't find the oracles in nethack3.0. how do you
explain it?

